  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "The atmospheric physicist James McDonald wrote a sharp attack on the Condon Committee, a University of Colorado study of UFOs whose final report, Scientific Study of Unidentified Flying Objects, was published on 31 October 1968. A researcher named Marik von Rennenkampff tells Michels to read everything McDonald wrote, starting with McDonald's piece Science in Default, which he calls 'a remarkable critique' of the committee. The point is that, if McDonald was right, the official study that dismissed UFOs in the late 1960s was badly flawed."
